=== STEP 3 — HYPOTHESES ===
- [HYP] Directory fetch_bulk unauthenticated batch amplification
  class: BUSLOGIC
  asset: https://ds-apip.threema.ch/identity/fetch_bulk
  confidence: 50
  reasoning: Accepted IDOR record shows POST fetch_bulk returns pubkeys for valid IDs, no auth, no rate limit (30 POSTs @1rps all 200); batch size is unconstrained in the confirmed surface. A large JSON array of IDs would be a cheap unauthenticated query against the backend.
  evidence_needed: response for batch of 1000+ IDs — 200 (no cap) vs 413/429 (cap/limit exists).
  verify_steps: PASSIVE: at ≤1 rps, three single POSTs with arrays of 1 / 100 / 1000 fabricated-format 8-char IDs; record status + body size + any RateLimit/Retry-After headers; no data modification, no real IDs.
  impact: request amplification / backend load from the public unauthenticated endpoint; severity low (no data beyond per-ID pubkey oracle already accepted).
  testability: PASSIVE
- [HYP] Broadcast challenge issuance carries no rate-limit once session+csrf valid
  class: AUTH
  asset: https://broadcast.threema.ch/en/login/passkey/start
  confidence: 48
  reasoning: Ceremony paths now fully resolved in live HTML; server issues SESSIONID+csrf on any unauth GET (observed); start POST is session+csrf-bound (orphaned csrf → 401) so cross-user leverage is absent. Only open question is whether a valid-session POST to start is throttled.
  evidence_needed: one valid-session POST to /en/login/passkey/start returning challenge + presence/absence of 429/RateLimit headers.
  verify_steps: PASSIVE (limited): single GET / to capture fresh csrf+SESSIONID, then ONE POST challenge (side-effect, deferred to next cycle); record status+headers; do not complete ceremony.
  impact: at most self-session challenge issuance / self-DoS; severity low.
  testability: PASSIVE
- [HYP] Gateway /api nginx-deny escape via method or extension
  class: AUTH
  asset: https://gateway.threema.ch/api/*
  confidence: 45
  reasoning: All 9 probed /api paths return uniform nginx 403 (146B) — a deny rule, not absence; nginx location blocks are commonly bypassable via method (TRACE/PROPFIND) or path tricks (/api//, /api/. , %2e, /API).
  evidence_needed: a /api subpath returning ≠nginx-403 (404/200/405 from the app layer) proving rule escape.
  verify_steps: PASSIVE: GET with path variants `/api//`, `/api/.`, `/api/%2e`, `/API/`, and HEAD/OPTIONS on `/api/v1/`; record status; ≤1 rps.
  impact: reach the gated control-plane route map; severity low until a real endpoint is exposed.
  testability: PASSIVE

